\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1  (void)\b slideDraggedImageTo:\b0 (NSPoint)\i aPoint\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Slides the image to \i aPoint\i0 , a specified location in the screen coordinate system. This method can be used to snap the image down to a particular location. It should only be invoked from within the destination\'27s implementation of \b prepareForDragOperation:\b0 \'d0in other words, after the user has released the image but before it\'27s removed from the screen.\
